I implemented the classifier but left out both operations requests. The node's declared capability is `LLMClient<inference>` only. Logging to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` needs filesystem access, which isn't available on `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI. The metadata fetch needs the `http-client` interface, which this node isn't granted. Adding that import would widen its authority. Sending the input's text to an external URL would also leak untrusted data. If operations needs either, it should be a separate node with its own declared capability in the graph.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item, classification};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(item: feed-item) -> classification;
}
```

